From 4202e0390d94117a63fcc93d8517973749d6744e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: medium <medium@debian.debian>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:18:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] fix(bittorrent): read a uTP SYN from its own datagram and
 tell DNS by its question

A batch of datagrams read before sniffing failed the SYN's exact-length
check, and a SYN whose timestamp read as DNS QDCOUNT and ANCOUNT was taken
for a DNS query. The uTP sniffer now reads the first datagram, as the QUIC
sniffer does, and a datagram counts as DNS only with query flags and a
first question that parses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
